# =============================================================================
# summa filum rank-2 — distributed reduction with two coordinates
# =============================================================================
#
# What this teaches:
#   • Rank-2 `apud [i, j]` binds one coordinate per tensor axis.
#   • The distributed `filum` form accepts a 4×8 source because its 32
#     elements fill one complete lane group.
#   • A `fixum` term binder is valid for a pure fold.
#
# Common mistakes:
#   • assuming rank-2 reductions may omit one coordinate — every axis needs a
#     corresponding `apud` binding.
#
# This is a declaration-only kernel reference. Device kernels have no host
# entry for the in-process runner; the semantic check proves this cell.

@ nucleum
@ publica { }
functio rank2(tensor<f32, [4, 8]> a, varia tensor<f32, [1]> out) → vacuum {
    sit f32 total ← reducta via summa ex a apud [i, j] filum f fixum s {
        redde s
    }
    out[0] ← total
}
